[
  {
    "id": "2043617551628865536",
    "author_id": "1759729576966590467",
    "text": "Testnet RPC latency issues have been resolved. All public endpoints are operating normally.",
    "created_at": "2026-04-13T09:09:27.543Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2052730441841479681",
    "author_id": "1889102044985790468",
    "text": "The testnet faucet is live. One claim per address per day.",
    "created_at": "2026-05-08T12:40:49.879Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2060671887466795010",
    "author_id": "1759729576966590467",
    "text": "Scheduled node upgrade complete. If you run your own node, update to the latest release at your convenience.",
    "created_at": "2026-05-30T10:37:18.061Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2069904968761446403",
    "author_id": "1889102044985790468",
    "text": "Faucet claims are temporarily paused while we deal with bot traffic. Back soon.",
    "created_at": "2026-06-24T22:06:16.184Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2070539904342265860",
    "author_id": "1889102044985790468",
    "text": "Faucet is back up. Same limits as before.",
    "created_at": "2026-06-26T16:09:16.623Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2086322575320256517",
    "author_id": "1759729576966590467",
    "text": "We are aware of intermittent timeouts on one public RPC endpoint. Investigating.",
    "created_at": "2026-08-09T05:23:58.612Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2086334813254946822",
    "author_id": "1759729576966590467",
    "text": "Resolved. Thanks for your patience.",
    "created_at": "2026-08-09T06:12:36.363Z",
    "conversation_id": "2086322575320256517"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120879701161906183",
    "author_id": "1315079665875390475",
    "text": "node's been up 11 days without a restart. don't jinx it",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T14:01:39.453Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120888834992869384",
    "author_id": "1413286777452990469",
    "text": "gm. second coffee, first deploy",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T14:37:57.128Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120893502745710601",
    "author_id": "1467282569427390474",
    "text": "gm. today is a cleanup day",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T14:56:30.007Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120897975362752522",
    "author_id": "1252748952992190470",
    "text": "anyone have a clean pattern for retrying txs when the nonce gets stuck? mine works but I don't trust it",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:14:16.362Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120904386687766539",
    "author_id": "1635430539065790465",
    "text": "finally got my node synced. took longer than I'd like to admit",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:39:44.941Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120905151607181324",
    "author_id": "1228106578131390480",
    "text": "track nonces locally, only resync from the node when a send fails. saved me a lot of pain",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:42:47.312Z",
    "conversation_id": "2120897975362752522"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120907919885570061",
    "author_id": "1252748952992190470",
    "text": "that's roughly what I had, good to know I'm not crazy",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:53:47.321Z",
    "conversation_id": "2120897975362752522"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120911345226846222",
    "author_id": "1611875327801790478",
    "text": "first time syncing a node on my old laptop. fans sound like a jet",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T16:07:23.986Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120919172276260879",
    "author_id": "1487576289900990471",
    "text": "weekend project: a dashboard that shows nothing but my own failed txs. humbling",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T16:38:30.100Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120926857784692752",
    "author_id": "1587595340806590466",
    "text": "trying to keep a dev journal this month. day 4 and already skipping",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:09:02.468Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120930150443356177",
    "author_id": "1413286777452990469",
    "text": "sent 3.17 MON to @felixmoves, we're square now",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:22:07.499Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120931690101051410",
    "author_id": "1559329087289790477",
    "text": "got it, thanks. landed before I even switched tabs",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:28:14.582Z",
    "conversation_id": "2120930150443356177"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120932100958294035",
    "author_id": "1168674968172990472",
    "text": "block explorer open in one tab, docs in the other, and still somehow wrong",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:29:52.538Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120936876534108180",
    "author_id": "1315079665875390475",
    "text": "the docs tab is always the wrong version too",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:48:51.124Z",
    "conversation_id": "2120932100958294035"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120942909524512789",
    "author_id": "1670219774163390473",
    "text": "reading the execution model docs again. it clicks a little more every time",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:12:49.501Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120944050974986262",
    "author_id": "1467282569427390474",
    "text": "1.0105 MON out. splitting funds across a few wallets so experiments don't touch the main one",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:17:21.644Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120950155713155095",
    "author_id": "1373424112236990479",
    "text": "sent 4.46 MON to a friend who couldn't get through the faucet queue",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:41:37.127Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120953887049879576",
    "author_id": "1000526998534590476",
    "text": "writing a thread on what I learned from a year of building on new chains. mostly: read the code, not the announcements",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:56:26.747Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120959228936425497",
    "author_id": "1611875327801790478",
    "text": "read the code, not the announcements. framing this",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:17:40.352Z",
    "conversation_id": "2120953887049879576"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120963824450768922",
    "author_id": "1228106578131390480",
    "text": "rpc tip: batch your reads. your node will thank you",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:35:56.008Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120965920378032155",
    "author_id": "1559329087289790477",
    "text": "the best feature of a fast chain is you stop making coffee while waiting",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T19:44:15.716Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120982354642571292",
    "author_id": "1487576289900990471",
    "text": "moved 4.264 MON into my hot wallet for the week",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:49:33.950Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120984070276485149",
    "author_id": "1315079665875390475",
    "text": "disk usage is the real final boss of running a node",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:56:22.989Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2120992814007816222",
    "author_id": "1373424112236990479",
    "text": "gas so low I forgot to check it. that's a habit I should keep anyway",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T21:31:07.657Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121004222409838623",
    "author_id": "1168674968172990472",
    "text": "parallel execution makes me rethink every assumption I had about ordering",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T22:16:27.632Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121010338455851040",
    "author_id": "1670219774163390473",
    "text": "same. I keep writing code that assumes the old world",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T22:40:45.811Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121004222409838623"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121017254938644513",
    "author_id": "1611875327801790478",
    "text": "favorite part of the week: answering newcomer questions in the discord",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T23:08:14.829Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121021449498497058",
    "author_id": "1413286777452990469",
    "text": "the thing nobody tells you about fast blocks is how fast your bugs ship too",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T23:24:54.890Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121025736093962275",
    "author_id": "1587595340806590466",
    "text": "this is too real",
    "created_at": "2026-11-12T23:41:56.894Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121021449498497058"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121034029759696932",
    "author_id": "1635430539065790465",
    "text": "reading through other people's deploy scripts is the best way to learn",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T00:14:54.258Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121041233573285925",
    "author_id": "1252748952992190470",
    "text": "shipped the retry fix. 300 lines down to 40",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T00:43:31.781Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121041348589490214",
    "author_id": "1467282569427390474",
    "text": "if your frontend shows a balance without a refresh button, users will assume it's broken",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T00:43:59.203Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121044899780857895",
    "author_id": "1467282569427390474",
    "text": "40 lines is the dream. what did you cut?",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T00:58:05.873Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121041233573285925"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121047318241710120",
    "author_id": "1252748952992190470",
    "text": "mostly my own cleverness",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T01:07:42.479Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121041233573285925"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121057526846296105",
    "author_id": "1559329087289790477",
    "text": "tipped 0.5 MON to someone who fixed my deploy script. pay your debuggers",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T01:48:16.400Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121060881886842922",
    "author_id": "1670219774163390473",
    "text": "small win today: my first contract that didn't need a redeploy",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T02:01:36.304Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121082067375067179",
    "author_id": "1000526998534590476",
    "text": "draft three of that thread. it keeps getting shorter",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T03:25:47.318Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121088732786823212",
    "author_id": "1487576289900990471",
    "text": "my rule: if a contract needs me to approve unlimited, I close the tab",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T03:52:16.476Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121091906843152429",
    "author_id": "1413286777452990469",
    "text": "same rule, learned the hard way",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T04:04:53.230Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121088732786823212"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121099202096762926",
    "author_id": "1587595340806590466",
    "text": "this week's plan: fewer tabs, more finished things",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T04:33:52.554Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121104197655433263",
    "author_id": "1635430539065790465",
    "text": "same plan, worse execution",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T04:53:43.588Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121099202096762926"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121105905194340400",
    "author_id": "1373424112236990479",
    "text": "unpopular opinion: most wallet UX problems are naming problems",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T05:00:30.697Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121109849559765041",
    "author_id": "1467282569427390474",
    "text": "'nonce' alone has caused more support tickets than any bug",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T05:16:11.107Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121105905194340400"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121116774552801330",
    "author_id": "1228106578131390480",
    "text": "my monitoring alert fired at 3am. it was the monitoring",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T05:43:42.154Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121129034541142067",
    "author_id": "1559329087289790477",
    "text": "moving apartments this week so if I'm slow to reply, that's why",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T06:32:25.163Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121135595762192436",
    "author_id": "1168674968172990472",
    "text": "good luck with the move",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T06:58:29.480Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121129034541142067"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121142278148296757",
    "author_id": "1413286777452990469",
    "text": "rewrote my indexer for the third time. it's smaller every time, which is either growth or giving up",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T07:25:02.685Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121154910909599798",
    "author_id": "1315079665875390475",
    "text": "jinxed it. restarting",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T08:15:14.570Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121158296832806967",
    "author_id": "1228106578131390480",
    "text": "it's always right after you say it out loud",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T08:28:41.837Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121154910909599798"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121166771323375672",
    "author_id": "1168674968172990472",
    "text": "spent an hour debugging what turned out to be a typo in an env var. classic",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T09:02:22.313Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121177251605614649",
    "author_id": "1611875327801790478",
    "text": "reminder that 'it works on my machine' is a status, not a solution",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T09:44:01.007Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121187788200579130",
    "author_id": "1670219774163390473",
    "text": "taking a break from screens. back tomorrow",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T10:25:53.127Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121201800426524731",
    "author_id": "1252748952992190470",
    "text": "code review is just two people agreeing to be confused together",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T11:21:33.902Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121218046144516156",
    "author_id": "1487576289900990471",
    "text": "late night reading other people's contracts is my version of true crime",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T12:26:07.183Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121224837561552957",
    "author_id": "1000526998534590476",
    "text": "ended up writing it as a blog post instead. tweets were too small for it",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T12:53:06.383Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121227948938203198",
    "author_id": "1635430539065790465",
    "text": "gm. quiet mempool this morning",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T13:05:28.193Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "2121229031177687103",
    "author_id": "1587595340806590466",
    "text": "always. coffee first though",
    "created_at": "2026-11-13T13:09:46.219Z",
    "conversation_id": "2121227948938203198"
  }
]
